<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Who this service has erased - decisions.md D39. The same table messaging has held since D32
        and booking gained in the same change, for the reason catalog needs it most: this is the
        service that DELETES. A saved list is removed outright rather than tombstoned, deliberately,
        and until D39 the act left a log line and an HTTP response that ended with the request.

        The table holds PSEUDONYMS ONLY. There is deliberately no column for the login: a register of
        erased people that names them is the thing erasure was asked to remove, and it would have to
        be kept forever for the check to keep working. Somebody who already holds a login can hash it
        and ask whether it is here; nothing goes the other way.

        One row per person, written once. erased_at is the fact an audit asks for and a retry must
        not move it - save() on an existing primary key would replace it with the date of the second
        run, which is exactly what D35 had to fix. The record of one fan-out ATTEMPT, of which there
        can be several, is booking's erasure_run table: a leg that fails cannot record its own
        failure, so that account can only live with the orchestrator.

        Hand-written, not generated from JDL. Regenerating catalog rewrites master.xml and DROPS this
        include, and the failure is SILENT: erasure goes on working, the receipt still reports what
        it redacted and deleted, and the estate simply stops keeping any record that it happened.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260902160000-1" author="healthconnect">
        <createTable tableName="erased_subject">
            <column name="pseudonym" type="varchar(64)">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="erased_at" type="${datetimeType}"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
        </createTable>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
